@startuml
' Yang Shuo with OpenAI Codex assistance. #641; Ernest's help and UI authors retained.
' Trace: MainWindow.handleHelp/executeCommand; CanonicalPeopleSession.getHelp;
' CanonicalCommandCatalog.getOverview/getUsage; ResultDisplay.setFeedbackToUser.
!include feature-sequence-style.iuml
participant "window :\nMainWindow" as W
participant "session :\nCanonicalPeopleSession" as S
participant "<<class>>\nCanonicalCommandCatalog" as C
participant "feedback :\nResultDisplay" as F

note over W, S
  Typed help uses the command route.
  F1 / Help menu call handleHelp().
  Preserve draft; Logic delegates to session.
end note
W -> S : execute(help [topic])\nvia Logic
S -> S : Normalize and validate topic
alt no topic
  S -> C : getOverview(load error)
  C --> S : available-command overview
else one known, available topic
  S -> C : getUsage(topic,\nprotected flag)
  C --> S : generated syntax and examples
else malformed, unknown or unavailable topic
  S -> S : Reject with usage guidance
end
S --> W : CommandResult or exception
opt help succeeded
  W -> W : Restore selected person by stable ID
end
W -> F : setFeedbackToUser(text)
F -> F : setText(text)\nScroll to top
note over S, F
  Unknown, unavailable or malformed topics return
  usage errors through the same feedback route.
  No operational write or separate help window.
end note
@enduml
